<title>GERMANY: SOCCER SHOWCASE-FACTS AND FIGURES FOR 1860 MUNICH V BAYERN.</title>
<headline>SOCCER SHOWCASE-FACTS AND FIGURES FOR 1860 MUNICH V BAYERN.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Facts and figures for Sunday's</p>
<p>German first division match between 1860 Munich and Bayern</p>
<p>Munich:</p>
<p>1860 Munich</p>
<p>Formed May 17, 1860.</p>
<p>Major honours: German champions 1966, German Cup winners</p>
<p>1942, 1964.</p>
<p>Ground: Munich Olympic stadium, capacity 69,267. Average</p>
<p>crowd 1995/96 - 32,105.</p>
<p>Coach: Werner Lorant.</p>
<p>President: Karl-Heinz Wildmoser.</p>
<p>Members: 15,000.</p>
<p>Record appearances: Radi Radenkovic 215, 1963-70.</p>
<p>Record goalscorer: Rudi Brunnenmeier 66 in 119 games</p>
<p>(1963-68).</p>
<p>Bundesliga record in the last decade: 1994/95-14, 1995/95-8.</p>
<p>----</p>
<p>Bayern Munich</p>
<p>Formed February 27, 1900.</p>
<p>Major honours: European champions 1974, 1975, 1976, European</p>
<p>Cup Winners' Cup winners 1967, UEFA Cup winners 1996. German</p>
<p>champions 1932, 1969, 1972, 1973, 1974, 1980, 1981, 1985, 1986,</p>
<p>1987, 1989, 1990 1994, German Cup winners 1957, 1966, 1967,</p>
<p>1969, 1971, 1982, 1984, 1986.</p>
<p>Ground: Munich Olympic stadium, capacity 69,267. Average</p>
<p>crowd 1995/96 - 59,766.</p>
<p>Coach: Giovanni Trapattoni (Italy).</p>
<p>President: Franz Beckenbauer.</p>
<p>Members: 49,800.</p>
<p>Record Appearances: Sepp Maier 473, 1965-79.</p>
<p>Record goal scorer: Gerd Mueller 365 in 427 games (1965-79).</p>
<p>Bundesliga record in the last decade: 1986/87-1, 1987/88-2,</p>
<p>1988/89-1, 1989/90-1, 1990/91-2, 1991/92-10, 1992/93-2,</p>
<p>1993/94-1, 1994/95-6, 1995/96-2.</p>
</text>
